# SP-15-09 originally listed every client-side route here as a
# `/path /index.html 200` "rewrite" rule. Cloudflare's own current docs
# (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/) are explicit
# that _redirects rewrites with a non-3xx status are NOT a supported
# feature — this worked when SP-15-09 verified it live, then stopped:
# every route below started returning a real 308 redirect to `/` instead
# of the SPA shell, confirmed via the deployment's own build log
# ("Found invalid redirect lines... Infinite loop detected") and via curl
# against the live deployment. Fixed at the incident dated 2026-08-03 with
# Cloudflare's actual documented mechanism instead: a Pages Function at
# /functions/[[path]].js, which serves index.html for any request that
# doesn't match a real static asset. _redirects rules are evaluated before
# Functions run, so the broken 200-status lines had to be removed here,
# not just superseded — leaving them would still 308 every route before
# the Function ever got a chance to run.
